        <referenceFunction amount="1.0" category="fuels" datasetRelatesToProduct="true" generalComment="Information was available only for a few mines. For the preparation of this module only amounts per tonne were available. The module has to be considered as a first approximation and may not reflect specific mines. Lifetime is assumed to be 30 years to take into account the lifetime of machinery. The main mine shaft is filled with concrete after the end of the lifetime, therefore the corrosion of the wood in the galleries is not accounted for. For defining the total production of a unit model mine, one million tonne per year has been estimated as an average worldwide (excluding small mines in China). This estimation includes open pit as well as underground mines. Therefore the total lifetime production of 30 million tonne shall be considered as a normalisation factor more than an actual average value for the real underground mines. Explosives are assumed to be used only during operation.;&#10;UUID: 695901ce-3394-363f-9833-e258e6b2f8a0" includedProcesses="This module includes an estimation of the most important construction materials and energy use for a model mine. The landuse for the infrastructure is also included. The machinery used for mining operation has been included in this module, because the relevant material use is not separated from the total material use in the available references." infrastructureProcess="true" localCategory="fuels" localName="Underground mine, hard coal" localSubCategory="coal\produced coal\mined coal\infrastructure" name="Underground mine, hard coal" subCategory="coal\produced coal\mined coal\infrastructure" unit="p"/>
